From 346f7ff179d14dde3dbdedc0c8e2356975eb3be0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:23:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dist): static requires + generated command manifest
 (unblock bun --compile)

Static bundlers (bun build --compile) need a static require graph, but the
registry discovered commands via fs.readdirSync + require(filePath), and
bin/forge.js + lib/commands/setup.js loaded lib modules via
require(path.join(packageDir, ...)).

- Add scripts/gen-command-manifest.js: scans lib/commands/*.js and emits the
  checked-in lib/commands/_manifest.js, which require()s every command by a
  static relative path (deterministic, timestamp-free, write-if-changed).
- _registry.js loadCommands: consume the manifest as the fast, bundleable path
  (applied for the canonical commands dir), keeping readdir auto-discovery as a
  dev/extension fallback so new command files load without regenerating.
- Convert dynamic require(path.join(packageDir,...)) sites in bin/forge.js and
  lib/commands/setup.js to static relative requires (packageDir retained for
  asset copying).
- Add drift guard test/structural/command-manifest-drift.test.js + colocated
  unit test test/commands/_manifest.test.js.
- Wire generation into build via package.json (gen:manifest, prebuild).

Refs 4a5a3c12-fda7-47c8-ac8b-f70347c39c13 (epic 6f11d483, step 1)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
